# The deb's DEBIAN/control. build-deb.sh drops these comment lines and fills
# in @VERSION@ and @INSTALLED_SIZE@.
#
# Depends, as in the Arch PKGBUILD: libasound2 and libdbus-1-3 are linked
# (sound, and the keyring's Secret Service client); the Wayland, X11 and
# xkbcommon libraries are loaded at run time by the window toolkit, so no
# tool would find them in the binary. libasound2 is libasound2t64 from
# Debian 13 and Ubuntu 24.04 on. libc6 is the glibc CI builds against.
#
# The keyring keeps the sign-in between launches; any Secret Service
# provider does (GNOME Keyring, KWallet, KeePassXC), and KDE has its own.
# Vulkan draws the window on the GPU; without it iced draws in software.
Package: aoide-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Virel0
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Virel0/aoide-linux
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libdbus-1-3, libxkbcommon0, libwayland-client0, libwayland-cursor0, libwayland-egl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxrandr2
Recommends: libvulkan1, mesa-vulkan-drivers | vulkan-icd, fonts-noto-cjk
Suggests: gnome-keyring | keepassxc
Description: native Jellyfin music client
 Aoide for Linux plays the music on your own Jellyfin server. It is the
 companion of the Aoide app for iPhone: with the Aoide plugin on the
 server, playlists and listening history sync between them.
 .
 It installs beside the Electron-based Aoide desktop app, as the command
 aoide-linux.
